C. Atomic loops -> magnetization current (volume curl M and surface M x n)
==============================================================================
PASS C1 uniform loops: every interior edge carries zero net current
PASS C1 uniform loops: right boundary +I (up), left -I (down), bottom +I (right), top -I (left)
PASS C1 boundary current direction on the right edge equals M x n (M out of the page)
PASS C1 boundary current direction on the top edge equals M x n (M out of the page)
PASS C1 boundary current direction on the left edge equals M x n (M out of the page)
PASS C1 boundary current direction on the bottom edge equals M x n (M out of the page)
PASS C1 surface current per unit length I/s equals M = I s^2/s^3
PASS C2 non-uniform M: the uncancelled edge current density equals -dMz/dx = (curl M)_y  —  edge J_y at x=0.51: -2.5050 vs -2.5050
PASS C2 M = M0 (x/d) z gives curl M = -(M0/d) y (uniform)
PASS C3 rod: M x r_hat = M phi_hat on the side (a solenoid winding, counter-clockwise seen from +z)
PASS C3 rod: no magnetization current on the end faces (M x (+-z) = 0)
PASS C3 [fig mag-loops-surface-current] rod with M up: right side current INTO the screen (y x x = -z)
PASS C3 [fig] rod with M up: left side current OUT of the screen (y x -x = +z)
PASS C3 [fig] explicit dl x R_hat: the two wires give B along +y (up) at the centre
PASS C4 thin layer: integral of curl M across the surface = M x n (n = +x)
PASS C5 interface magnetization current n x (M1 - M2) = (face of 2: M2 x n) + (face of 1: M1 x (-n))
PASS C6 twin: rho_sb = -n.(P1 - P2) = P2.n + P1.(-n)
